@page "/docs/software"
@{ ViewData["Title"] = L["Software"]; }
<div class="wrap page with-side">
  <partial name="_DocsNav" />
  <div>
    <h1 style="font-size:34px">@L["Software"]</h1>
    <p class="muted">@L["Windows 10 or 11 is required."]</p>
    <div class="grid two" style="margin-top:24px">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">@L["For pilots"]</div>
        <h3>SkyPilot</h3>
        <p class="muted small">@L["The client for Microsoft Flight Simulator 2020 and 2024, X-Plane 11 and 12 and Prepar3D v4–v6: network connection, flight plan from the website, messages, nearby controllers. It finds the running simulator by itself."]</p>
        <p class="sim-list"><span class="badge accent">MSFS 2020 / 2024</span> <span class="badge accent">X-Plane 11 / 12</span> <span class="badge accent">Prepar3D v4–v6</span></p>
        <p class="muted small">@L["X-Plane: copy the XPlanePlugin/SkyPilot folder from the SkyPilot folder into X-Plane/Resources/plugins. To see other pilots, add a CSL model package to it, for example the free Bluebell (see CSL-README.txt there)."]</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/chatgpt82628163-pixel/SkyPilot/releases/latest">@L["Download SkyPilot"]</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">@L["For controllers"]</div>
        <h3>Network-ATC</h3>
        <p class="muted small">@L["Radar: EuroScope and .natc sectors, handoffs, SID/STAR, departure and arrival lists, STCA, plugins."]</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/chatgpt82628163-pixel/Network-ATC/releases/latest">@L["Download Network-ATC"]</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top:16px">
      <div class="eyebrow">@L["Voice"]</div>
      <h3>@L["Radio voice is built in"]</h3>
      <p class="muted small" style="margin:0">@L["Both programs talk on the radio themselves: nothing else to install. Choose the microphone, speakers and push-to-talk key or joystick button in the settings. You hear stations tuned to your frequencies within radio range; weak signals sound noisy, as on a real VHF radio. The voice server uses UDP port 3782."]</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
